{
 "id": "HST-03",
 "name": "battery-gauge",
 "version": 3,
 "title": "Battery gauge",
 "summary": "A battery icon filled to a host-supplied battery level (0-100) that turns red below 20%, with the percentage under it.",
 "prompt": "Make a battery widget that fills to the phone's battery percentage and turns red when it drops below 20%.",
 "level": 3,
 "family": "HST",
 "capabilities": {
  "primary": [
   "host.variables",
   "data.condition"
  ],
  "secondary": [
   "data.expression",
   "draw.shapes",
   "draw.stroke",
   "text.dynamic"
  ]
 },
 "use_cases": [
  "gauge",
  "widget"
 ],
 "form_factor": "widget-2x2",
 "keywords": [
  "battery",
  "charge",
  "power",
  "level indicator",
  "low battery",
  "status",
  "battery percentage",
  "charge level"
 ],
 "components": [
  "BatteryIndicator"
 ],
 "teaches": [
  "Take the level from an exported host float (resources.variables battery, default 76) and pass it to BatteryIndicator as level \"@battery\"",
  "Turn the fill red below 20% with the component's lowAt (warnAt 20 too, so there is no amber step)",
  "Show \"76%\" as one centred text under the icon with textMerge of a textFromFloat(clamp(0, 100, @battery), flags 4) and \"%\""
 ],
 "snippets": [
  {
   "pointer": "/resources/variables",
   "shows": "host.variables",
   "note": "battery, set by the host"
  },
  {
   "pointer": "/root/column/children/0",
   "shows": "data.condition",
   "note": "BatteryIndicator: level @battery, red below lowAt 20"
  },
  {
   "pointer": "/root/column/children/1",
   "shows": "text.dynamic",
   "note": "textMerge(textFromFloat(clamp(0, 100, @battery), flags 4), \"%\"), centred"
  },
  {
   "pointer": "/root/column/children/1/text/value/id1/value",
   "shows": "data.expression",
   "note": "clamp(0, 100, @battery): the value goes last"
  }
 ],
 "inputs": {
  "variables": {
   "battery": {
    "type": "float",
    "meaning": "battery charge, percent",
    "default": 76,
    "min": 0,
    "max": 100,
    "step": 1
   }
  },
  "clock": null,
  "touch": false
 },
 "check": {
  "describe": "Default: a green fill at 76% and \"76%\". variables {battery: 15}: a short red fill with a ! and \"15%\". Resized, the background fills the box and the battery shrinks to the narrow width, centred over its percentage.",
  "render": {
   "variables": {
    "battery": 15
   }
  },
  "renders": [
   {
    "name": "narrow",
    "width": 130,
    "height": 200
   },
   {
    "name": "wide",
    "width": 320,
    "height": 200
   }
  ]
 },
 "related": [
  "HST-01",
  "HST-05"
 ],
 "pitfalls": [
  "batteryLevel() (system variable 38) is an rcj/json2rc extension: the Java parser rejects it (\"Unknown token in expression\") and Android's RemoteContext defines no battery id, so a portable document takes the level from a host variable",
  "clamp takes the value last: clamp(0, 100, @battery). clamp(@battery, 0, 100) returns 0 for any level",
  "textFromFloat pads to `whole` digits with a leading space (\" 15\"), which shifts centred text; flags 4 drops the padding",
  "BatteryIndicator's own percentage sits beside the icon and is cut in a narrow box: pass showPercent false and put the number under it"
 ],
